 <blockquote>
 <p><strong>Patients:</strong> this Privacy Policy covers our website and messaging programs. Your protected health information is governed separately by our <a href="notice-of-privacy-practices.html">Notice of Privacy Practices</a>, which describes your rights under HIPAA and how CoreFlow Rx uses and discloses health information for treatment, payment, and health care operations.</p>
 </blockquote>

 <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
 <p>CoreFlow Rx is a specialty infusion pharmacy. This policy explains what information we collect through coreflowrx.com and our text messaging programs, how we use it, and how we protect it.</p>

 <h2>2. Information we collect</h2>
 <p><strong>Information you give us directly</strong></p>
 <ul>
 <li><strong>Provider and practice information</strong> — name, practice name, NPI, practice address, phone, fax, and email, submitted through our referral or contact forms.</li>
 <li><strong>Patient information</strong> — submitted by a referring provider through our referral form, including name, date of birth, contact information, insurance information, diagnosis, and prescribed therapy. This is protected health information and is also governed by our Notice of Privacy Practices.</li>
 <li><strong>Mobile number and messaging consent</strong> — when you enroll in a messaging program.</li>
 <li><strong>Employment information</strong> — if you apply through our careers page.</li>
 <li><strong>General inquiries</strong> — anything you send us through our contact form, by email, or by phone.</li>
 </ul>
 <p><strong>Information collected automatically</strong></p>
 <ul>
 <li><strong>Website analytics.</strong> We use Plausible Analytics, which is privacy-focused, does not use cookies, and does not collect or transmit personal identifiers. It records aggregate page views and referral sources only.</li>
 <li><strong>We do not use advertising or tracking pixels.</strong> There is no Google Analytics, Meta Pixel, or LinkedIn Insight tag on this site, and none on any page in our referral pathway.</li>
 </ul>

 <h2>3. How we use your information</h2>
 <p>We use the information we collect to:</p>
 <ul>
 <li>Receive, verify, and process patient referrals</li>
 <li>Confirm insurance benefits and obtain prior authorization</li>
 <li>Schedule, coordinate, and document infusion services</li>
 <li>Communicate with referring providers about referrals they submitted</li>
 <li>Communicate with patients about their appointments and treatment</li>
 <li>Respond to inquiries and provide customer support</li>
 <li>Evaluate employment applications</li>
 <li>Meet our legal, regulatory, accreditation, and recordkeeping obligations</li>
 <li>Maintain the security and integrity of our systems</li>
 </ul>
 <p><strong>We do not use your information for marketing or promotional purposes, and we do not sell it.</strong></p>

 <h2>4. How we share information</h2>
 <p><strong>We do not sell, rent, or trade your personal information. We do not share it with third parties for their own marketing or promotional purposes.</strong></p>
 <p><strong>Mobile information.</strong> <em>No mobile information will be shared with third parties or affiliates for marketing or promotional purposes. All other categories of information exclude text messaging originator opt-in data and consent; this information will not be shared with any third parties.</em></p>
 <p><strong>Service providers.</strong> We use vendors to operate our pharmacy and this website — including our referral intake platform, pharmacy management system, and nursing partners. These vendors process information only to perform services for us, only under written agreement, and may not use it for their own purposes. Where they handle protected health information, they do so under a HIPAA Business Associate Agreement.</p>
 <p><strong>Treatment, payment, and operations.</strong> As a pharmacy, we share health information with your insurer, prescribing provider, nursing agency, and others involved in your care, as permitted by HIPAA and described in our <a href="notice-of-privacy-practices.html">Notice of Privacy Practices</a>.</p>
 <p><strong>Legal requirements.</strong> We may disclose information where required by law, regulation, subpoena, or court order, or to protect the safety of any person.</p>

 <h2>5. How we protect information</h2>
 <p>We maintain administrative, physical, and technical safeguards designed to protect personal and health information, consistent with the HIPAA Security Rule. This includes encryption of information in transit, access controls limiting information to staff who need it, written agreements with vendors who handle protected information, and workforce privacy and security training.</p>
 <p>No method of transmission or storage is completely secure. <strong>Please do not send protected health information to us by unsecured email or through our general contact form.</strong> Use our secure referral form or call us at <strong>{{ site.phone }}</strong>.</p>

 <h2>6. How long we keep information</h2>
 <p>We retain information for as long as needed to provide services and to meet legal, regulatory, accreditation, and pharmacy recordkeeping requirements, after which it is securely destroyed.</p>

 <h2>7. Your choices and rights</h2>
 <ul>
 <li><strong>Text messages</strong> — opt out at any time by texting <strong>STOP</strong>, as described in our <a href="terms.html">Terms &amp; Conditions</a>.</li>
 <li><strong>Email</strong> — unsubscribe from any non-essential email using the link in the message, or contact us.</li>
 <li><strong>Health information rights</strong> — your rights to access, amend, restrict, and receive an accounting of disclosures of your protected health information are described in our <a href="notice-of-privacy-practices.html">Notice of Privacy Practices</a>.</li>
 <li><strong>Questions or concerns</strong> — contact our Privacy Officer using the information below.</li>
 </ul>

 <h2>8. Children</h2>
 <p>This website is not directed to children, and we do not knowingly collect information from children through it. Where CoreFlow Rx provides services to a pediatric patient, that patient's health information is handled under our Notice of Privacy Practices and applicable law.</p>

 <h2>9. Third-party links</h2>
 <p>Our site may link to other organizations. We are not responsible for their privacy practices, and this policy does not apply to them.</p>

 <h2>10. Changes to this policy</h2>
 <p>We may update this policy. Material changes will be reflected in the effective date above.</p>

